# These findings come from pip's *vendored* dependencies, listed in
# `pip/_vendor/vendor.txt`. pip bundles its own private copies of these packages
# (setuptools, msgpack) for its internal use only. This container never invokes
# pip at runtime — the application runs from the pre-built virtualenv — so these
# vendored copies are not reachable or exploitable here.
#
# The actually-installed setuptools is upgraded to a patched version in the
# Dockerfile; only pip's internal vendored copy still reports the CVE.
#
# Reassess when pip ships patched vendored dependencies.

# setuptools (pip-vendored) — Path Traversal in PackageIndex
CVE-2025-47273

# msgpack (pip-vendored) — Out-of-bounds read on Unpacker reuse
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
